{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/worldmodule\/event"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"inheritsFrom","kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"title":"Inherits From"},{"type":"conformingTypes","kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/RemovedComponent"],"title":"Conforming Types"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Event","kind":"identifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s8SendableP","text":"Sendable","kind":"typeIdentifier"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Use events to decouple the code that notices something from the code that responds to it:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a physics step sends a collision, and separate damage and sound systems each read it. Declare","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"an event as a type that conforms to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Event"},{"text":", send it with ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/send(_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":", and read it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/readEvents(_:by:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"code":["struct Collision: Event { var first: Entity, second: Entity }","enum DamageReader {}","","var world = World()","let ship = world.spawn(Health(current: 3))","let asteroid = world.spawn(Health(current: 1))","world.send(Collision(first: ship, second: asteroid))","","for collision in world.readEvents(Collision.self, by: DamageReader.self) {","    world[Health.self, of: collision.first].current -= 1","}","print(world[Health.self, of: ship])","\/\/ Prints \"Health(current: 2)\""],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Events wait in the world’s "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Events"},{"type":"text","text":" resource until "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/updateEvents()"},{"type":"text","text":" drops them,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so senders and readers don’t need to run at the same moment. Unlike an "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/EntityEvent"},{"type":"text","text":", an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"event isn’t aimed at an entity and runs no code when sent."}]}]}],"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Event"},"metadata":{"title":"Event","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Event","kind":"identifier"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"Events.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/ECS\/blob\/main\/Sources\/WorldModule\/Events.swift#L27"},"roleHeading":"Protocol","symbolKind":"protocol","modules":[{"name":"WorldModule"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Event","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","externalID":"s:11WorldModule5EventP"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Sending-Events","identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Events","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/EventsView"],"generated":true,"title":"Sending Events"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A type that describes a message one part of a p